WEBVTT

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.270
Hey, Onpu-chan.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:10.630
How did you do on that Japanese test we got back today?

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.360
Those problems were hard!

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.470
Don't tell anyone, but I got a 64.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.540
Onpu-chan, what did you get?

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:56.050
We're supposed to send e-mails to our sister school in Okayama today, right?

00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:00.260
Nah, I think it's a class for Seki-sensei to learn about computing.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.280
Alright, can it.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:08.280
Looks like Seki-sensei doesn't really know how to use a computer.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.060
Can anyone help her?

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.940
I-I can't do it.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:16.150
Doremi-chan, don't you girls have a computer? You know how to use them, right?

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:19.970
No, that's not a computer, it's an old man.

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:22.620
Is there anyone here that knows how to use a computer?

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.240
Now's my chance.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.290
I can show her my good side.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:34.480
Onpu's E-Mail was a Love Letter?

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.220
Um, can I try?

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:43.370
Gouji, you know how to use one?

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:44.200
Yes.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.270
Alright then, go for it.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:50.850
Wow!

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.610
She's looking at me!

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:57.200
That's amazing, Nakata-kun. How did you get so good at using computers?

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:03.030
My dad gave me an old computer, so I know how to send e-mails and stuff.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.550
Wow!

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.620
By the way, what's an e-mail?

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:16.140
Um, to put it simply, e-mails are letters that you can send instantly.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:19.200
You can use them to chat with other people.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:24.140
You can become friends with anyone in Japan, or even people from all over the world.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:29.390
Just type up your letter and then click here.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.460
Thank you, Nakata!

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.220
Our class can go smoothly now.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:36.190
I-It's nothing.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.740
But can't you also make friends by calling them or sending them letters?

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:49.300
You can see the ocean from the roof of our school.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.450
I'm sure the ocean over at Okayama is gorgeous.

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:54.620
That works.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:58.520
Yes, then you click this button to send the e-mail out.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:03:59.520
I see.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.930
Well then... Segawa, see if you can do what Nakata did.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.320
Okay!

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:09.490
Oh? I don't think it's Segawa-san's turn yet.

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:13.390
Since I'm prettier, I should be the one to do it.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.560
W-What?

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.030
Okay, class ends here today.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.230
Hey, Nakata, you can do other things with computers, right?

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:28.120
Yes.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.240
For example...

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.290
It's Onpu-chan!

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.410
A CD?

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.230
It's probably a game.

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:37.630
I didn't know Onpu-chan was on a CD.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.620
This is a CD-ROM.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:44.190
It's not like a regular CD. It contains pictures and music.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:49.350
You can make it a photo album with voices.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:53.270
Segawa Onpu in Hawaii!

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.800
H-Hawaii!?

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:57.840
Wow, she's been to Hawaii before?

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.060
Onpu-chan!

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:01.110
Have you really been to Hawaii?

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:02.920
What is with them?

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:06.450
I've been there like 20 times, at least!

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:17.940
Onpu-chan!

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:27.010
She's coming this way...

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:32.850
Onpu-chan!

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:37.480
Please...

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:40.820
Let me talk!

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.520
Onpu-chan!

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.240
Ah, Kotake-kun, what is it?

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.120
Actually, it's about Hawaii...

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.410
Hey, Onpu.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.520
What?

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:58.640
Your fanclub's homepage received some e-mails.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.610
Don't you want to respond to them?

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:02.470
E-mail?

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:06.890
People sent you fan letters via their computers.

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.550
You better read them and respond.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.600
That's too troublesome, so I'll pass.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:17.670
I don't know how to use a computer, and that homepage was put up by the record company.

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:20.730
So, why should <i>I </i> respond to those e-mails?

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.650
What are you saying!?

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.680
If you don't care for your fans, you'll never make it as an idol!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.610
Then you can respond to them, Majo Ruka.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.560
Ah, I can't!

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.850
Then let Hehe do it.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:36.120
Well, I have work to do, so I'll leave the rest to you.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:48.900
How did I get stuck doing this?

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.640
This is too hard.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.170
I got it.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:57.060
From your lovely Segawa Onpu.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:02.440
I'll just copy the same letter and send it out to everyone.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.650
Okay, all finished.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:10.570
I'll be waiting at Misora Park,

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:10.740
so be sure to come <3

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:11.240
You better come!!

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.490
From your lovely Segawa Onpu <3

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:16.910
Onpu-chan sent me a reply!

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.830
Onpu-chan!

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:22.330
Onpu! I love you too!

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.500
Let go of me! I'm Onpu's boyfriend!

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:28.380
Onpu-chan, I'm looking forward to tomorrow!

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:29.750
Tomorrow?

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:35.390
Onpu-chan! Onpu-chan!

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:38.590
Something doesn't seem right.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.400
Nakata-kun, sorry I'm late.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.280
Have you been waiting?

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:51.530
N-Nope, I just got here.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.700
I'm sorry, work took a bit longer than expected.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:57.530
That's fine, you couldn't help it.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:00.880
Oh, Nakata-kun, you're so nice!

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.090
Jeez...

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:05.460
Wow, look at the time.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.880
I'll also get her autograph today.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:15.330
Go find the Bad Cards <i>right now!</i>

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:17.950
You must find them before noon today!

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:18.810
Is he broken?

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:22.370
You idiots! I can't break.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:25.820
I want to turn back right now!

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:30.610
Or else... Or else I can't go on a date with Onpu-chan!

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.070
Oh wow, he is broken.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:35.720
Looks like you don't believe me.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.460
Then I'll show you evidence.

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.250
This is a love letter from Onpu-chan!

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:42.870
What the?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.050
"Hello, this is Onpu."

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:48.700
"It's a bit sudden, but I really loved your e-mail."

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:52.240
"Could this be love at first sight?"

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:55.990
"I'll be waiting at Misora Park this Sunday at noon,"

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:57.520
"so be sure to come."

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:59.030
"You better come!!"

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:00.970
"From your lovely Segawa Onpu."

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:02.320
How about that?

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:03.180
Pretty awesome isn't it?

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:07.400
Is that really an e-mail from Onpu-chan?

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:08.230
Yes.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.110
It seems a bit off from her usual personality.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:12.070
What?

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.280
You wrote that yerself, didn't ya?

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.800
You idiots!

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:20.480
This was from her response from my letter to her homepage!

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:24.750
Please, my apprentices, take me to the park!

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:31.690
H-Harukaze-san.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.380
Nakata-kun!

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:37.850
Hey!

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:40.580
Why are you all dressed up?

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.720
Ah, are you going on a date?

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:46.390
Well, it's a bit embarrassing, but yes.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:49.170
Eh? It kinda suits ya, Nakata-kun.

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:51.400
It's all thanks to that e-mail.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:52.610
E-mail?

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:58.280
I sent so many e-mails, and I finally got a response saying that she'll see me.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:01.000
Hey, who's the girl?

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.070
Well...

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:03.580
It's Onpu-chan.

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:05.990
Onpu-chan?

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:09.510
Onpu-chan's into guys like Nakata-kun?

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:10.940
How out of character.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.700
You are a fan of Onpu-chan too, right?

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:18.840
Yeah, but I've never seen ya talk to her at school though.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:22.650
Yes, but I e-mailed her a lot.

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:27.650
And e-mail makes it easier to say difficult things.

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:28.800
Oh no, I'm gonna be late.

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:30.310
I'm gonna be late!

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:31.880
Okay, see you later!

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:36.360
So what Oyajiide said...

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.800
That's somethin' else.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:40.020
We were fooled!

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:41.320
Oyajii!

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:45.620
You dirty old man! Stop lying to us!

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:48.410
What should we do?

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:49.220
Let's go home.

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:38.190
Onpu-chan!

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.140
How can ya sit there drinkin' tea!?

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:45.220
Oh, what's wrong, girls?

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:47.660
Nothing's wrong with us!

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:52.940
Because of your e-mails, so many of your fans are gathered at the park!

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:56.900
Oh, that. That's all Hehe's fault, so it's causing problems for me too.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:12:00.900
But you seem pretty calm about all of this.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.460
Well, it's nothing, really.

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:05.370
I just have to erase their memories using magic.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.020
What are you saying!?

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:11.620
If you use such magic on that many humans, there will be consequences!

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.360
Huh? But I have my magic charm.

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:15.840
That's not the problem!

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:19.710
We'll help you, so we can all do something.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.720
Anyway, we gotta get to the park!

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.900
Hey, what are you doing?

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:26.420
Onpu-chan...

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:28.820
Your e-mail promised, but you're not here.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.020
What!?

00:12:30.570 --> 00:12:31.980
What's going on!?

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:35.770
Onpu-chan's love letter was for me.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.420
What did you say?

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:40.190
Onpu-chan's e-mail was for me!

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:41.280
Onpu-chan's...

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:42.190
E-mail?

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:43.680
No, that was for me!

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:45.510
Back off, you fakes!

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:49.290
No, that e-mail was definitely for me!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:50.560
No way...

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:53.120
I sent her tons of e-mails every day!

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.750
What happened to Onpu-chan!?

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.460
This is scary...

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:59.660
I think you should go apologize to them.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:01.400
Apologize how?

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:06.760
Just go up and tell them the e-mails were sent by a fairy named Hehe?

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.000
How's that sound?

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.360
Guess you've got a point...

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:14.130
If Onpu-chan were to suddenly appear, I don't know what will happen.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.190
Well then, leave it to me.

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:22.440
Pirika Pirilala Poporina Peperuto!

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:25.620
Turn me into Onpu-chan's manager!

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:30.240
Okay then, me too.

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:36.250
Paipai Ponpoi Puwapuwa Puu!

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.240
Turn me into a bodyguard!

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:45.010
We'll calm them down, so come out after that.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:46.380
Go for it!

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:52.350
Everyone, thank you for coming here today.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.060
Who are you?

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:57.390
I-I'm Onpu-chan's manager.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:00.900
And this is Onpu-chan's bodyguard.

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:02.840
Nice to meet you.

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:05.360
Everyone, please calm down.

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:07.790
How can we calm down?

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:09.840
Give us Onpu-chan right now!

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:12.990
You guys are suspicious! Let's take them down!

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:14.750
W-W-W-Wait!

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:23.520
Where's Onpu-chan?

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.590
Oh no, I hafta do somethin'!

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.510
This is why I wanted to erase their memories.

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:34.560
Pururun Purun Famifami Faa!

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.140
Erase their memories!

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:36.980
No!

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:41.600
Onpu-chan! How many times have we told ya not to use that kinda magic?

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:43.170
Then what should I do?

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:46.240
I dunno... I dunno! But...

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:52.000
Why are you so stubborn when this doesn't even concern you?

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:55.240
No matter what punishment I get, it has nothing to do with you girls.

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:56.910
That ain't true!

00:14:58.100 --> 00:14:59.490
Think about it.

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:03.470
Why are those fans gathered here today?

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:07.340
It's because they all love you.

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:10.510
Hey, did you hear Onpu-chan's voice just now?

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:14.540
Yeah, it came from the bushes over there.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:21.900
Eh?

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.860
Someone's stopped time!

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.570
Goodness, you really give me so much trouble.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:27.920
Majo Ruka.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:30.030
Come on, let's get out of here.

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:31.440
R-Right.

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:35.700
W-Wait, Onpu-chan!

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.660
You girls run too!

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:39.870
No! We can't run!

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:43.180
Wait, you have to calm them down first!

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:44.540
Onpu-chan!

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.700
Hey, Onpu, what are you doing?

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:00.920
We have to go!

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:01.820
I can't.

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:02.770
Huh!?

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:04.650
Huh?

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:08.650
Everyone!

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:12.910
O-Onpu-chan!

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:15.820
Onpu-chan!

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:17.880
I'm sorry.

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:20.620
I never read any of your e-mails.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.120
Eh?

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:28.960
I don't know how to use a computer, so I had a company employee respond to them.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:32.550
And the responses were too much.

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:35.970
I don't know how to apologize to all of you.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.010
But... Um...

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.310
I'm really sorry.

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:48.520
Since you all came, I'll just hold an autograph session here.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:52.000
So cute!

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.200
It's okay! Don't worry about it!

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:57.320
Onpu-chan's such an honest and considerate girl!

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:05.990
Onpu-chan, hurray!

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:14.620
Will she be okay?

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:16.980
Well, I guess.

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:19.830
Hey, where's Nakata-kun?

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.940
She never read them...

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:38.490
That's impossible...

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:41.180
Screw it all!

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:42.660
Nakata-kun!

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:44.600
Harukaze-san.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:47.370
Nakata-kun, aren't you going to get her autograph?

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.080
What're ya talkin' about, Doremi-chan?

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:53.550
He's our classmate, so he can get her autograph anytime he wants.

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:54.920
Her autograph...

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:59.550
Forget about her autograph, she's never even spoken to me before.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.080
She's never spoken to you?

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:04.220
So you're saying that you've never spoken to her either?

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.420
It's hilarious, isn't it?

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:12.320
I sent so many e-mails and finally got a response, a fake one too.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:15.440
And Onpu-chan never even read any of them.

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:18.350
But it's fine now.

00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:20.680
I don't need this anymore.

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:31.020
A Bad Item!

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:36.630
So the reason he's never spoken to her before was because of that CD-ROM!

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.090
I... think so too.

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:46.220
Pirika Pirilala Carefreely!

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:52.780
Paipai Ponpoi Flexibly!

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:57.950
Pameruku Laruku Proudly!

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:10.560
Magical Stage!

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:19.200
Come out, Bad Card!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:30.640
Doremi-chan.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:31.480
Right.

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:41.030
You know, was this all really caused by the Bad Item?

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:49.110
Is there something else you want?

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:49.790
This.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.640
I don't want it anymore.

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:53.000
You can have it if you if you like.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:54.210
But...

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:55.720
It's okay.

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:58.600
I'm not a fan of her anymore.

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:00.550
Ya sure give up easily, Nakata-kun.

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:06.720
Yeah, you've never even spoken to her before, and now you're disliking her.

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.470
That's unfair for Onpu-chan.

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:10.150
Leave me alone!

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:13.060
You don't understand how I feel!

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:14.360
You're right, we don't.

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:20.440
We don't understand this at all, because you've never even tried anything.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:28.130
I think e-mail is very cool, since you can make friends with anyone in the world, right?

00:20:28.130 --> 00:20:32.040
You can talk with people you've never seen before. I think that's very cool.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:36.320
So even though I don't know how to use a computer, I'm still your friend.

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:41.200
It's not only Doremi-chan.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:43.200
Me and Ai-chan too.

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:47.030
And I think Onpu-chan is also your friend.

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:48.940
We're all classmates, after all.

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:52.220
And of course, Onpu-chan is always right there with you.

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:59.900
Don't worry, once you talk to her, she'll become your friend.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:02.290
'Kay, we'll see ya at school.

00:21:31.110 --> 00:21:31.640
Um...

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:37.060
G-Good morning, Onpu-chan.

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:39.560
Good morning, Nakata-kun.

00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:56.960
I did it!

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:02.490
Listen, listen.

00:22:02.490 --> 00:22:06.200
Papa became the conductor of the new overnight express train.

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:07.660
Eh? You mean that brand new one?

00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:09.220
Yes, and I also get to ride on it.

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:10.080
The new overnight express!

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:11.100
That's great!

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:15.750
But because of work, I haven't seen Papa for a long time, so I'm looking forward to Saturday.

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:18.820
Eh? But don't you have an audition on Saturday, Onpu-chan?

00:22:18.820 --> 00:22:21.240
Don't worry, I can make it with magic.

00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:22.200
Later!

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:23.320
Ojamajo Doremi!

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:26.330
I Want to Meet Papa! The Dream Aboard the Overnight Express.

00:22:26.330 --> 00:22:28.940
Happy! Lucky! For all of you!
